<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Waldheim affair</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1986</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Waldheim affair was a controversy over the wartime past of Kurt Waldheim, former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secretary-general-of-the-united-nations">Secretary-General of the United Nations</a>, during his successful campaign for the Austrian presidency in 1986. Revelations showed that he had concealed his service as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wehrmacht">Wehrmacht</a> officer in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, where war crimes were committed. A commission of historians found no proof of personal guilt but criticised his silence, and the affair pushed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> to confront its role in Nazi crimes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/waldheim-affair.jpg" alt="Waldheim affair" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gotfryd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurt_Waldheim_UN_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
